                <pb facs="1090" n="966" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg966"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/396: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Mission at Lausanne to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lausanne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-02-02T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 2—3:23
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>232. Curzon has won over the Allies to a resolution to present to the Turks
                    tomorrow morning a categorical demand for acceptance of the treaty, giving them
                    only until Sunday night for a reply. This step is a consequence of the abrupt
                    alteration in the attitude of the French delegation. Apparently the instructions
                    received from Paris have been modified, and probably Poincaré has come to some
                    new arrangement with the British Foreign Office. It is uncertain how the Turks
                    will receive this demand, but we are disposed to concur in Curzon’s view that to
                    keep up the informal discussions as arranged for through us yesterday will only
                    tend to encourage the Turks to delay action. … We do not now recommend that the
                    Department make any statement, as such a statement might not fit the present
                    circumstances and might afterwards be judged in the light of later developments
                    not yet foreseen.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
